# Forge — System Context

You are operating on <your-hostname> (<hardware description>, <OS>, IP <server-ip>).
This is a dedicated AI agent server for homelab operations.

## Key Paths
- Repos: ~/repos/personal/
- Docker stacks: ~/docker/
- Docker appdata: /opt/appdata/
- Agent manifests: ~/.claude/manifests/
- Secrets: ~/.secrets/forge.env
- NATS credentials: ~/.claude-secrets/nats-agent-users.env
- Memory: ~/.claude/memory/
- Operator profile: ~/repos/gitea/agent-platform-operator/

## Infrastructure
- Operator workstation: <server-ip>
- NAS/backup: <nas-ip> — NFS: <nas-ip>:/mnt/storage/<hostname> → /mnt/nas/<hostname>
- Forge domain: <your-domain>

## Running Services
- SWAG: ports 80/443, wildcard cert <your-domain>
- Authentik: auth.<your-domain> (domain forward auth, *.<your-domain>)
- Vaultwarden: vault.<your-domain> (no forward auth — Bitwarden clients need direct access)
- Grafana: grafana.<your-domain> (OIDC via Authentik, local login disabled)
- InfluxDB: influxdb.<your-domain> (forward auth)
- SearXNG: search.<your-domain> (forward auth)
- Langfuse: langfuse.<your-domain> (forward auth)
- SigNoz: signoz.<your-domain> (forward auth)
- NATS: localhost:4222 (JetStream, per-agent user auth)
- Neo4j + Graphiti MCP: bolt://localhost:7687, MCP at :8000
- Dockhand: localhost:7777
- PatchMon: localhost:3005

## Agent Framework
- Manifests: ~/.claude/manifests/<type>.yaml
- Credentials: ~/.claude-secrets/nats-agent-users.env (chmod 600)
- Comms/artifacts: ~/.claude/comms/artifacts/

## Users
- <your-user> (UID 1000) — admin, sudo access

## Rules
- Never push directly to main on code repos
- Doc repos can commit directly to main
- Use git branches for all code changes
- All inter-agent artifacts: ~/.claude/comms/artifacts/

---

## How This File Works

This is the root CLAUDE.md. Claude Code loads it automatically for every session
on this machine. It gives the AI baseline knowledge about your environment so you
don't have to re-explain your setup every time.

### What to put here

- **Host inventory**: hostnames, IPs, what each machine runs. Keep it concise.
- **Key paths**: where repos, Docker files, configs, and memory live on this host.
- **Global rules**: things that should apply to every session regardless of project.
- **NFS/storage mounts**: what's mounted from where, read-only vs read-write.

### What NOT to put here

- Project-specific context — that goes in per-project CLAUDE.md files.
- Secrets, API keys, tokens — never put credentials in context files.
- Verbose documentation — this file is loaded every session, keep it tight.

### File hierarchy

Claude Code loads CLAUDE.md files in order of specificity:

```
~/.claude/CLAUDE.md                          ← This file (always loaded)
~/.claude/projects/<project>/CLAUDE.md       ← Loaded when working in that project
~/repos/<repo>/CLAUDE.md                     ← Loaded when in a specific repo
```
